\section{Adapter Architecture Search (AAS) Details}
\label{app:aas_details}

The AAS loop maintains a population of 20 adapters over 12 generations (${\sim}240$ evaluations, 3-epoch fitness probes). Elitism preserves the top 2; an LLM variant generates candidates in the code space $\mathcal{G}_\text{code}$. Template-based generation achieves 100\% validity (vs.\ ${\sim}75\%$ for LLM). The 5 canonical pooling heads used by RR-MoA (mean, last-token, max, attention, Conv1d) were identified as the most frequent structural motifs across the ${\sim}1{,}200$ candidate adapters explored.

